<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Saigon (1862)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1862">1862</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cochinchina-campaign">Cochinchina campaign</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-saigon-1874">Treaty of Saigon</a>, signed on 5 June 1862, ended the first phase of the French conquest of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vietnam">Vietnam</a>. Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tu-duc">Tự Đức</a> of the Nguyễn dynasty ceded the three eastern provinces of Biên Hòa, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gia-dinh">Gia Định</a> and Định Tường, with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ho-chi-minh-city">Saigon</a> and the islands of Poulo Condore, to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, paid an indemnity, opened ports to trade and allowed Catholic missionaries to preach. These lands became the core of French Cochinchina.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-saigon-1862.jpg" alt="Treaty of Saigon (1862)" width="320" height="430" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Adolf Bastian · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:IndoChina1867,_Cochinchina.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
